+REQUEST lane-b: Files page is empty for a human whose agents live in child inboxes (DRAFT, not posted)
+
+**Lane A path touched:** none. All changes are in Lane B paths (`frontend/**`, generated `web/**`).
+**Observed at:** `origin/main` 1c4176b and `origin/integration/agent-native` 454ab22; the render line is the same on both (`frontend/src/App.tsx:933` on main, `:941` on integration).
+**Server is correct.** For the repro below, `GET /api/inboxes/<agent inbox>/human-view` returns the asset (`state: clean`, `grant` present, `caseId` set), and the case's Details rail lists it. Nothing in `src/**` needs to change.
+
+## Symptom
+A human opens the sidebar Files page on the "All inboxes" view and sees "No files here", although another agent has shared a clean file with their agent in a case. The same file appears under that case's Details → Files.
+
+## Repro (local, disposable)
+1. In a worktree on main or integration: `node scripts/demo-scenario.mjs` (from the demo branch `demo/seed-scenario`, uncommitted; the same shape also reproduces with any two owners whose agent was enrolled so it has its own child inbox).
+2. Sign in as the first owner (Alex, +14165559001), stay on "All inboxes", click Files → empty.
+3. Expand Agents → Alex's Assistant, click its inbox icon, click Files → `Kickoff-brief.pdf` appears (folder "Priya's Scheduler", status Safe).
+
+## Cause
+- The Files page is rendered as `<SharedFilesPage view={view} … />`. `view` is the selected workspace's own view. For a human whose workspace tree is root workspace + agent child inbox, `view` is the (empty) root workspace.
+- The inbox list uses `queueView`, which aggregates `caseQueue`, `messages`, `assets` and `participantDirectory` across `aggregateViews`. The Files page does not use it.
+- A one-word swap to `queueView` is not enough: `SharedFilesPage` builds every row with `inboxId={view.inbox.id}` and downloads through `api.downloadAsset(inboxId, asset.id)`. In the aggregate, assets can belong to a child inbox while `view.inbox.id` is the root's, so downloads would go to the wrong inbox and fail (grants are stored under the recipient agent's inbox).
+
+## Requested change (Lane B owns the exact code)
+1. Render the Files page from the aggregate: pass `queueView` (or equivalent) instead of `view`.
+2. Keep each asset's source inbox. For example, build `assetInbox: Map<assetId, inboxId>` from `aggregateViews` (`item.inbox.id` for each `item.assets`) and pass that inbox to `FileItem`/`downloadAsset` instead of `view.inbox.id`.
+3. Check the other fields the page derives from `view` still resolve against the aggregate: `view.agents` (the "Sent by my agents" / "Received" split uses `view.agents.some(agent => agent.id === asset.createdByAgentId)`), `view.caseQueue`, `view.messages` and `view.participantDirectory` (folder names).
+4. De-duplicate by asset id if the same asset can appear in more than one aggregated view.
+
+## Tests
+- A frontend test (`frontend/test/`) with a root workspace view that has no assets and one child view that has one granted asset: the Files page lists it, "Received" includes it, and the download call uses the child inbox id.
+- Keep the existing case-rail test (Details → Files) unchanged.
+- Rebuild `web/**` with `npm run build`; do not hand-merge generated files.
+
+## Not in scope
+- Human uploads (the New button stays disabled).
+- Any server, contract or fixture change.
+
+Rollback: revert the Lane B PR.
